# Integer128 remainder by zero

Takes 100 modulo zero to verify the failure surfaces as a language-level
division-by-zero error with exit code 1 instead of producing a value.

>>> source
const dividend: int128 = 100
const divisor: int128 = 0

const remainder: int128 = dividend % divisor
print(remainder)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: division by zero

<<< exit
1
